  "description": "SCOUT's nodes in Curio. The Raster Calculator runs one operation over rasters on one grid: add, subtract, multiply, divide or choose, cell by cell, or a raster's statistics as a table of one row. Rasterize Buildings, SCOUT's building rasterizer ported from SCOUT (urban-toolkit/scout), turns a buildings layer into the zoom-16 height tiles SCOUT's Deep Umbra shadow model reads, side by side in one raster in metres that an Autark map draws. Seven Vega-Lite charts connect after a Compare Scenarios node, for forms its Chart tab does not draw: lines with a band, curves by group, bars with error bars, ensemble strips, stacked bars with totals, donuts and a weighted matrix. Each reads the node's stacked table and draws each scenario in its box's color, in the order of the node's inputs; the columns it plots are text widgets in its Widgets tab.",
  "id": "curio.scout",
  "license": "MIT",
  "name": "Scout",
  "permissions": [],
  "publisher": "Curio",
  "readOnly": true,
  "templates": [
    {
      "category": "computation",
      "description": "One operation over rasters on one grid. Connect the rasters to its input circles, in order; its code names the operation. Cell by cell: add, subtract, multiply or divide input_0 and input_1, or choose, which takes input_1 where input_0's class is one of the codes it names and input_2 elsewhere; a cell that is nodata in an input the operation reads there is nodata in the result, and rasters on different grids are refused. Statistics: the mean, median, minimum, maximum and count of a raster's cells, nodata left out; its code can keep only the cells that meet a condition, such as a value under 1.08, on the raster itself or on a second raster on input_1, on the same grid, used as a mask: a test of the mask's values or a set of them. The output is the result: a raster an Autark map draws, or the statistics as a table of one row, which Compare Scenarios charts.",
      "editor": "code",
      "engine": "python",
      "hasCode": true,
      "hasGrammar": false,
      "hasWidgets": true,
      "iconRef": "fa-solid:calculator",
      "id": "raster-calculator",
      "inputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "[1,3]",
          "types": [
            "RASTER"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "label": "Raster Calculator",
      "behavior": "code",
      "outputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "1",
          "types": [
            "RASTER",
            "DATAFRAME"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "paletteOrder": 0,
      "source": "sources/raster-calculator.py",
      "dataflowCategories": {
        "dataTypes": [
          "Rasters"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "computation",
      "description": "SCOUT's OSM vector to raster: draws each building's height into 256 by 256 map tiles at a zoom level, 8-bit gray where 255 is the maximum height, in EPSG:3395. Input: a buildings GeoDataFrame with a column of heights in metres. Output: one RASTER of the tiles side by side, heights in metres, band band_1, for an Autark map and for Accumulated Shadow (model.scout.deep-umbra), which runs SCOUT's Deep Umbra shadow model on it. A tile SCOUT writes no file for, because no building is near it, is no data.",
      "editor": "code",
      "engine": "python",
      "hasCode": true,
      "hasGrammar": false,
      "hasWidgets": true,
      "iconRef": "fa-solid:city",
      "id": "rasterize-buildings",
      "inputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "1",
          "types": [
            "GEODATAFRAME"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "label": "Rasterize Buildings",
      "behavior": "code",
      "outputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "1",
          "types": [
            "RASTER"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "paletteOrder": 1,
      "source": "sources/rasterize-buildings.py",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "name": "attribute",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Height column",
          "default": "height"
        },
        {
          "name": "zoom",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "Zoom level",
          "default": 16,
          "options": {
            "min": 1,
            "max": 20,
            "step": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "max_height",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "Maximum height",
          "default": 550,
          "options": {
            "min": 1,
            "step": 1,
            "units": "m"
          }
        }
      ],
      "dataflowCategories": {
        "dataTypes": [
          "Rasters"
        ]
      }
    },
